## 5. Simulation Results

Fig. 14a: Grover on reduced SIMON, single $(M,C)$ pair, shows two peaks in the
measurement histogram at $K=[0,0,1,1,1,0]$ and $K'=[1,1,1,0,0,0]$.

Fig. 14b: with a second $(M_1, C_1) = ([0,0,1,1,0,1], [1,1,0,0,1,1])$ pair,
the histogram peaks uniquely at $K$; the collision key $K''=[0,0,1,0,0,1]$
appears in the single-pair case but is eliminated by the intersection.

## 6. Conclusion

We have built a reversible Qiskit implementation of the SIMON block cipher
family and demonstrated Grover-based key search on a reduced instance.
Success probability agrees with the theoretical $\sin^2((2k{+}1)\theta)$
Grover formula, saturating at $k = (\pi/4)\sqrt{N/M}$.

